# apps/cli — environment (the `wego` CLI; issue #883, M1)
# Copy to `.env.local` for the complete source-CLI runtime, start the local apps
# through `bunx portless`, then run `wego login`. Every value is orthogonal: auth
# points at STAGING, while the API points at the named local apps/api that verifies
# those staging tokens and proxies to staging upstreams. Keep auth and API in the
# SAME environment when retargeting - a staging token sent to the prod API (or
# vice versa) is rejected with 401. Bun loads this file relative to the CLI
# module, so source `wego` works from any cwd. Everything here is PUBLIC: the
# client_id is a public PKCE client (no secret) and is identical in staging/prod.

# --- Runtime target (foundations#74 rung 2) ---
# One switch for the whole bundle below: `--target prod|staging|local`, or this
# var. Left UNSET on purpose, which means `prod` - the safe end has to be what
# you get when you say nothing. Naming a non-prod target overrides the four
# values in this file for that run, sends no usage event, and keys the stored
# credentials by the auth host it logged in against. The four values below stay
# the source-run default, so nothing here changes if you never name a target.
# `local` is the exception: it keeps WEGO_API_URL below (portless names it per
# worktree), but only when that is a host on this machine - a remote URL exits 2
# rather than letting `--target local` talk to a deployed backend.
# `wego info target` prints the resolved answer.
# WEGO_TARGET=staging

# --- OAuth client (Authorization Code + PKCE) ---
WEGO_AUTH_AUTHORIZE_URL=https://auth.wegostaging.com/user-auth/v2/users/oauth/authorize
WEGO_AUTH_TOKEN_URL=https://auth.wegostaging.com/user-auth/v2/users/oauth/token
# Seeded `wego` CLI public client_id (required for `login`; same in stg + prod).
WEGO_CLI_CLIENT_ID=251815b9647317f4895122fd4924b7d44541d8fcc27be528435e3ad9bbf7e1ee

# --- Resource server ---
# Portless named URL: the proxy owns the numeric port. For plain `bun dev`, use
# `WEGO_API_URL=http://localhost:3001` instead. Linked worktrees resolve their prefixed URL
# at command time:
#   WEGO_API_URL="$(bunx portless get api)" wego whoami
WEGO_API_URL=https://api.localhost

# --- Loopback redirect (RFC 8252) ---
# Declared explicitly and set to their code defaults, so a straight
# `cp .env.local.example .env.local` leaves nothing hidden behind a default
# (12-factor: complete config). The seeded client registers
# http://127.0.0.1/callback with any ephemeral port, so these are exactly the
# values the CLI would use anyway — no override is required. Change them only for
# a differently-registered client: set WEGO_CLI_REDIRECT_PATH empty for a
# bare-origin redirect_uri, or set a fixed WEGO_CLI_REDIRECT_PORT for a client
# that registers a specific loopback port instead of the RFC 8252 port override.
WEGO_CLI_REDIRECT_PORT=0
WEGO_CLI_REDIRECT_PATH=/callback

# --- Requested OAuth scopes (code default; quoted so the space-separated value
# survives strict dotenv parsers such as direnv's) ---
WEGO_CLI_SCOPES="openid profile users"

# --- Token store location (optional) ---
# Left unset so the default applies: ~/.config/<command>/credentials.json (or
# $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/<command>/credentials.json when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set). The
# <command> segment is the name the binary was invoked as – the install's
# identity, so any two installs coexist without sharing a login. It is "wego" for
# a source run and for a default install, "wegostaging" for the staging binary,
# and "wego-next" for a second install named that. Unlike the
# values above it has no portable literal (the default is homedir-derived), so it
# stays commented rather than declared. To override, set an absolute path: Bun's
# loader does NOT expand ~ in .env values (it stays literal), and it DOES expand
# $VAR — so a literal "$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/…" with XDG_CONFIG_HOME unset expands to
# "/wego/credentials.json".
# WEGO_CREDENTIALS_PATH=
